course: dictionary
lesson: 412
title: Appoint and appointment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To appoint someone is to choose them officially for a job or role. «Members of the House of Lords, called peers, are appointed, not elected.» Here appointed means chosen for the job, not picked by votes.
explain: The word also has a formal meaning: to appoint a time or place is to decide it. «The meeting was held at the appointed time.» The appointed time is the time that was set. Ask yourself: is someone being chosen, or is a time being decided?
explain: The noun appointment has two common meanings: a job given to someone, or a booked time to see someone, like a doctor or dentist. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: To appoint means to choose someone officially for a job or role.
fact: «Appointed» can also mean decided in advance, as in «at the appointed time».
fact: An appointment can be a job given to someone, or a booked time to see a doctor or dentist.
fact: In Canada, «the Senate is appointed, not elected», while MPs in the House of Commons are voted for.
fact: Appoint is a verb: appoint, appoints, appointed, appointing.
exercise: «Canada's Senate is appointed, not elected.» What does appointed mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Voted for by everyone in the country | *Chosen officially, not voted for | Lost
exercise: The class teacher will appoint a new class captain on Monday. What does appoint mean? | *Choose someone officially for a role | Remove someone from a role | Wave goodbye to someone | Ask a question about a role
exercise: «The meeting was held at the appointed time.» What does appointed mean here? | Painted | Late and unhappy | *Decided and set in advance | Forgotten
test: The head teacher will appoint a new librarian. Which word means the same as appoint? | Lose | *Choose | Hide
test: «Dad has a dentist appointment on Friday.» What is an appointment here? | A holiday | *A booked time to see the dentist | A dentist's drill | A job at the dentist
exam: What does appointed mean in «The club appointed Mia as captain»? | Cancelled | *Chosen officially for the role | Painted | Lost
